ef 17592186406767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406770 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406770 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406770 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186406761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406770 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bc7e9e1f-8201-5457-9ae8-866cb0a50e5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406771 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406771 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161810" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406771 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406771 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+vw \\\\ {v}^{2} \\\\ w+v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186406771 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "84951e54-c705-5b01-85eb-275b777e397c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406771 #edb/ref 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+vw,\\,y(u,v,w)={v}^{2},\\,z(u,v,w)=w+v.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & w & v \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}2v & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(2v-0) \\\\  & =2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2v & =0 \\\\ v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $v=0$ defines the plane $v=0,$ i.e., $uw$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186406772 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406772 #edb/ref 1069 "q-39710" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406772 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406772 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+vw,\\,y=2-uv,\\,z={v}^{2}-w.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406772 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9eac1497-79c1-5ed3-be68-00cfa0edfef5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406772 #edb/ref 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & w & v \\\\ -v & -u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u(-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-u & 0 \\\\ 2v & -1\\end{vmatrix}+(-v)(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}w & v \\\\ 2v & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u(u-0)+v(-w-2{v}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}-2{v}^{3}-vw.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186416646 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186416647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416646 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186416648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416646 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186416649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416646 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416646 #edb/ref 1045 "The Jacobian of a Three-Dimensional Transformation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416646 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186416648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416646 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416646 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416646 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "44c9ee16-7425-5861-8f66-16a66ae948b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416647 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416647 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1059b764-2977-50ff-bfe0-2e03c6d8a3b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416647 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416648 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416648 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8e074033-7ddf-5114-859f-8aff01ee8989" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416648 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416649 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d544d535-b361-5b73-8a3a-da1f8a5abef8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416649 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186281337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424148 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424148 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424148 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0584ff70-04f9-53f4-b918-d40c95661794" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424151 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/re